# --- docs ---
# `docs/` used to be ignored wholesale, which meant nothing written about this
# project ever reached the group. The opposite extreme is no better: personal
# planning notes and viva revision are working material, not deliverables, and
# they go stale the moment the code moves.
#
# So: ignore the folder, then re-admit the one document the team actually
# needs. Note this is `docs/*` and not `docs/` — git will not look inside an
# excluded DIRECTORY, so a negation under `docs/` would never match.
docs/*
!docs/trybe-api-reference.md

# `tests/` was also ignored and is not any more. Tests are a deliverable.

# postman/ stays partly ignored: the exported collections carry environment ids
# and bearer tokens from live sessions. regenerate.py rebuilds them from
# scratch, so nothing is lost by leaving them out.
postman/*.json

# local .env backups — never commit
.env.backup*
